From 15fb2bf0165a3d47a1aed2dfd5ff3b03b7672eda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:20:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] XHCI X5: INTx delivery, live root ports, plan close-out

The INTx pin (IRQ 10, INTA#) is now driven: asserted while IMAN.IP &
IMAN.IE & USBCMD.INTE hold, level-triggered on change (pic_set_irq,
the AHCI S5 convention), deasserted by HCRST. The guest's handler
clears IP via IMAN RW1C and warns that a missed ack livelocks the
IRQ; vectors pin both of its ack paths (IMAN RW1C and ERDP-EHB) and
both gates (IE=0 / INTE=0 keep the pin down with IP latched;
re-enabling re-asserts) against the PIC line state itself.

Root port 1 carries the shared stick whenever a disk image is
attached (the uhci_port_attached rule): PORTSC reads CCS +
High-Speed + PP. At the RUN 0->1 edge the port latches CSC and posts
a Port Status Change event (type 34, port id in Parameter[31:24]) --
the signal the guest's hotplug handler actually peeks the ring head
for, since by its own measurement QEMU never raises USBSTS.PCD (we
raise that too). Port Reset and Warm Reset complete synchronously,
consistent with the rest of the engine: PR/WPR never read back set,
PED comes up with PRC/WRC latched and a second status-change event.
Transfers are not gated on PED (the guest resets before addressing;
stated in the plan).

tests/test_xhci.c gains three groups (22 total): the full port
lifecycle (presence/speed, the RUN-edge CSC+PSC, the RW1C-clear
vector deferred since X1, reset-to-enabled, enumeration over the
live port), the IRQ mask/ack matrix, and a determinism replay (the
same doorbell script after HCRST gives a byte-identical event
stream). NC: src/xhci.c reverted to X4 -> 21 failures. Gates: make
test, make test-sanitize, both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green.

This closes the XHCI plan (X0-X5, patches 0076-0081): a QEMU-parity
xHCI (1b36:000d) with register file, command ring, slot/EP contexts,
control + bulk + interrupt transfers against the shared MSC device,
live ports and INTx -- every phase measured against the AuraLite-OS
driver's own contract.
